      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1358273752,
      "text": "Eucalyptus gamophylla, commonly known as warilu, blue-leaved mallee, twin-leaf mallee, twin-leaved mallee or blue mallee, is a species of mallee that is native to Western Australia, South Australia and the Northern Territory. It usually has smooth bark, mostly only juvenile leaves arranged in opposite pairs, flower buds in groups of three, whitish flowers and cylindrical to barrel-shaped fruit that is four-sided in cross-section."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Eucalyptus gamophylla",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eucalyptus_gamophylla",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 218910275,
      "text": "Eucalyptus gamophylla est une espèce de plantes à fleurs du genre Eucalyptus et de la famille des Myrtaceae. C'est un arbre ou un arbuste originaire du centre de l'Australie."
    }
